    fix(site): a no-JS enquiry submit now lands the lead instead of losing it
    
    The enquire form had no method or action. With scripts absent or failed, submit
    did the browser default: a GET back onto the same page - the lead in the query string, nobody told, nothing captured.
    
    The form now POSTs to /site-enquiry (token in a hidden field, HMAC-verified),
    reusing chat_enquiry: same validation, dedupe, durable outbox as the JSON path.
    The inline script still preventDefaults where it runs. python-multipart added:
    the round-trip test 500d without it.
    
    4 new tests incl. a TestClient round trip; browser-proven: the original no-JS
    reproduction now POSTs and lands on Enquiry sent. 2,102 tests.

